-- title:
--   Ordinary line and tame shape at p=3, weights 3≤ k≤ p+1
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p=3$, let $N\geq 1$ with $p\nmid N$, let $S\subseteq\mathbb{N}$ be finite with $p\notin S$, and let $k$ be an integer with $3\leq k\leq p+1$, given also as a natural number $k_n$ with $k_n=k$. Write $\mathbb{T}$ for `heckeAlgebra N k S`, the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$. Let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and $\theta\colon\mathbb{T}\to F$ a ring homomorphism with $\theta(T_p)\neq 0$, and let $\rho\colon\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})\to\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ be a monoid homomorphism such that: $\rho$ is trivial on the pointwise stabiliser of some finite-dimensional intermediate field $L$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$; for every $u\neq 0$ in $F^2$ some $\rho(\sigma)u$ lies outside $F\cdot u$; and for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\neq p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$, one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho(\sigma)=\theta(T_\ell)$ and $\det\rho(\sigma)=\ell^{\,k_n-1}$. Fix moreover a valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit. The conclusion is twofold. First, for all $\ell,A,\sigma$ as above the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell^{\,k_n-1}$. Second, there is a vector $v\neq 0$ in $F^2$ such that: $F\cdot v$ is stable under $\rho(\sigma)$ for every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$; $(\rho(\sigma)-1)w\in F\cdot v$ for every $w\in F^2$ and every $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$; $(\rho(\sigma)-\theta(T_p))w\in F\cdot v$ for every $w$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ acting as $x\mapsto x^{p}$ on the residue field of $P$; and $\rho(\sigma)v=a^{\,k_n-1}v$ whenever $\sigma$ lies in that inertia subgroup and $a\in\mathbb{N}$ is such that $\sigma\mu=\mu^{a}$ for all $p$-th roots of unity $\mu$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Here the exponent $k_n-1$ is formed in $\mathbb{N}$.
--
--   This is the ordinary-line statement of Deligne, in the form used by Gross and by Edixhoven: a $p$-ordinary mod $p$ eigensystem of weight $k$ with $3\le k\le p+1$ and level prime to $p$ forces the attached irreducible representation to be reducible on the decomposition group at $p$, with an unramified quotient on which Frobenius acts by $\theta(T_p)$ and a stable line on which inertia acts through the $(k-1)$-st power of the mod $p$ cyclotomic character. It is the $p=3$ instance of the general statement, and feeds the level-and-weight bookkeeping at the prime $3$ through [`GaloisRep.exists_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_eq_three`](thm.html#GaloisRep.exists_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_eq_three).
